From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AML: an HDR change sets the mode again only where it changes
 the link

Any change of HDR type forced a full mode set, even at an unchanged
resolution and rate. Stopping an HDR10 film at 2160p24 tore the HDMI
link down and up again with nothing on it different: the kernel had
already sent the SDR metadata, and the colour format and depth it picks
follow the HDR type only on the Dolby Vision path. Each such re-set
costs the sink chain a relock, and one of them left an LG TV with no
signal until the next mode set.

The force is now kept where the HDR type does decide the link: Dolby
Vision on either side, or a conversion the user set (the VS10 modes and
the forced SDR/HDR output).

The same rule covers frame-sequential 3D in HFR VRR, where Kodi learns a
film's HDR type from its first configured picture, a moment after the
stereo mode has entered HFR VRR: an HDR10 film no longer sets 1080p165 a
second time 0.3 s later, resetting the TV, the eARC link and the
receiver once more. The 3D output patches carried that as a special
case of their own.

Where the window is kept, the new HDR type is recorded, so the next
change is judged from it.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/xbmc/utils/AMLUtils.cpp b/xbmc/utils/AMLUtils.cpp
index 07003fc375..393f7abc86 100644
--- a/xbmc/utils/AMLUtils.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/utils/AMLUtils.cpp
@@ -333,6 +333,20 @@ bool aml_convert_to_dv_by_vs_engine(StreamHdrType hdrType)
   return ((convert_to_dv && !!user_convert_to_dv && !!dv_user_enabled) == 1);
 }
 
+// Only the Dolby Vision engine and a forced conversion tie the HDMI colour
+// format to the HDR type; otherwise the kernel signals HDR frame by frame.
+static bool aml_hdr_type_sets_link(StreamHdrType hdrType)
+{
+  return hdrType == StreamHdrType::HDR_TYPE_DOLBYVISION || aml_convert_to_dv_by_vs_engine(hdrType) ||
+         aml_convert_to_sdr_by_vs_engine(hdrType) || aml_convert_to_hdr_by_vs_engine(hdrType) ||
+         aml_convert_to_sdr(hdrType) || aml_convert_to_hdr(hdrType);
+}
+
+bool aml_hdr_change_needs_mode_set(StreamHdrType from, StreamHdrType to)
+{
+  return from != to && (aml_hdr_type_sets_link(from) || aml_hdr_type_sets_link(to));
+}
+
 bool aml_video_started()
 {
   CSysfsPath videostarted{"/sys/class/tsync/videostarted"};
diff --git a/xbmc/utils/AMLUtils.h b/xbmc/utils/AMLUtils.h
index 755201720e..fcea3e78a6 100644
--- a/xbmc/utils/AMLUtils.h
+++ b/xbmc/utils/AMLUtils.h
@@ -67,6 +67,7 @@ bool aml_convert_to_hdr(StreamHdrType hdrType);
 bool aml_convert_to_sdr_by_vs_engine(StreamHdrType hdrType);
 bool aml_convert_to_hdr_by_vs_engine(StreamHdrType hdrType);
 bool aml_convert_to_dv_by_vs_engine(StreamHdrType hdrType);
+bool aml_hdr_change_needs_mode_set(StreamHdrType from, StreamHdrType to);
 bool aml_video_started();
 int aml_amdv_wait(StreamHdrType hdrType);
 void aml_set_3d_video_mode(unsigned int mode, bool framepacking_support, int view_mode);
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
index 23771eab17..35aa536d6a 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@ bool CWinSystemAmlogicGLESContext::CreateNewWindow(const std::string& name,
   bool nativeGUI = CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent()->GetSettings()->GetBool(CSettings::SETTING_COREELEC_AMLOGIC_DISABLEGUISCALING);
 
   StreamHdrType hdrType = CServiceBroker::GetWinSystem()->GetGfxContext().GetHDRType();
-  bool force_mode_switch_by_hdr = (m_hdrType != hdrType);
+  bool force_mode_switch_by_hdr = aml_hdr_change_needs_mode_set(m_hdrType, hdrType);
   // Without HDMI 3D, a stereo mode changes the output only by entering or
   // leaving HFR VRR.
   bool force_mode_switch_by_stereo_mode =
@@ -197,6 +197,7 @@ bool CWinSystemAmlogicGLESContext::CreateNewWindow(const std::string& name,
       !force_mode_switch_by_stereo_mode && !force_mode_switch_by_fs3d_rate)
   {
     CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "CWinSystemAmlogicGLESContext::{}: No need to create a new window", __FUNCTION__);
+    m_hdrType = hdrType;
     // the surface stays as it is, stacked HFR VRR GUI included
     int eyeWidth = 0;
     int eyeHeight = 0;
